  "notes": "The rap-rock crossover of the lane, and the research names the departure in as many words: \"distorted electric-guitar riff as the lead line — the defining departure from snap's synth palette\". That is the one place this model breaks its parent's rule. ⛔ **The archetype's whole design is a motif above C5 so the hook survives a phone speaker; this model's melody starts at 62, thirteen semitones lower, because the record's lead is a guitar in guitar register.** It is a deliberate, sourced exception, not a drift — and everything else about the kit stays snap, which is what makes the exception legible. `session.scales` leads with `minor_pentatonic` and carries `blues` at weight 4 for the ♭5 inflection the research names; `timbreHint` is `guitar`, which is the closest hint in the shipped vocabulary to a distorted electric. The rock crash on section starts is `percs.lanes` `crash` at `downbeat` placement — the placement matters, because a cymbal sprinkled across the 16ths reads as a mistake rather than an accent. ⚠ **`placement` is per block, not per lane**, so the snap and tambourine sitting beside the crash are pinned to the beats too. That is the lesser of the two errors available: beat 3 is a beat, so a snap on the downbeats lands where the research puts it, where an offbeat sprinkle would have put the crash between the beats. ⚠ **Confidence is medium and the research says which half is sourced**: the producer credit (Jason \"Pit\" Pittman), the \"rap rock\" genre label and the certification are documented; the tempi are [LOW-CONF], so `session.bpm` 142–162 is the inference. ⚠ The harmony is a static `i` under a pentatonic riff; the `i–VII` and `i–VI` families are **INFERRED** at low weight and are what let the chord part reach the variety a producer is owed. What actually carries it is `chordDurationBeats` [2, 10] and a 28-semitone voicing register. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
